From: OpenWrt community
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx6q-marsboard: configure the AR8035 PHY

The MarS Board never passed Ethernet traffic: the link came up but no
frame crossed the PHY, in U-Boot and in Linux alike. The U-Boot side
fixup (ported from the vendor BSP and the known-good SolidRun microSOM
configuration for the same PHY) proved that programming the PHY fixes
it. Since the PHY node carries reset-gpios, Linux resets the PHY at
probe time and all register programming done by the bootloader is lost,
so the kernel has to redo it through the at803x driver DT properties:

- qca,clk-out-frequency: the CLK_25M pin is wired to the ENET_REF_CLK
  pad; program it to 125 MHz.
- qca,disable-smarteee: keep SmartEEE off, matching the U-Boot fixup
  (SmartEEE caused link glitches on AR803x).

The RGMII rx/tx delays for phy-mode = "rgmii-id" are applied by the
at803x driver itself, so they need no DT property.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/imx/imx6q-marsboard.dts	2026-09-09 00:10:40.898970118 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nxp/imx/imx6q-marsboard.dts	2026-09-09 00:10:40.899420516 +0800
@@ -121,6 +121,15 @@
 		/* Atheros AR8035 PHY */
 		rgmii_phy: ethernet-phy@4 {
 			reg = <4>;
+			/*
+			 * CLK_25M feeds the ENET_REF_CLK pad; program it to
+			 * 125 MHz and keep SmartEEE off, like the working
+			 * U-Boot fixup for this board. The RGMII delays for
+			 * phy-mode = "rgmii-id" are applied by the at803x
+			 * driver itself.
+			 */
+			qca,clk-out-frequency = <125000000>;
+			qca,disable-smarteee;
 			interrupts-extended = <&gpio1 28 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
 			reset-gpios = <&gpio3 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 			reset-assert-us = <10000>;
